From 840f033f16eed568392f3daad8bab33af11b04e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:09:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rk3588): save and restore the PHP CRU clock gate
 separately

clk_gate_con_save() stores PHP_CRU CLKGATE_CON0 in clk_save[j] without
advancing j. The first secure CRU gate register then lands in the same
slot and overwrites it. clk_gate_con_restore() has the same off-by-one,
so on resume from system suspend PHPCRU_CLKGATE_CON0 is written with the
value saved for SECURECRU_CLKGATE_CON0.

PHPCRU_CLKGATE_CON0 holds the APB clock gates of the three PCIe/SATA/USB3
combo PHYs (pclk_pcie_combo_pipe_phy0..2). If they come back gated while
the kernel still considers them enabled, the first PHY register access
after resume stalls the bus.

Advance the index after the PHP gate register in both functions.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 plat/rockchip/rk3588/drivers/pmu/pmu.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/rockchip/rk3588/drivers/pmu/pmu.c b/plat/rockchip/rk3588/drivers/pmu/pmu.c
index 1a6394d..dcff02b 100644
--- a/plat/rockchip/rk3588/drivers/pmu/pmu.c
+++ b/plat/rockchip/rk3588/drivers/pmu/pmu.c
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ void clk_gate_con_save(void)
 	for (i = 0; i < CRU_CLKGATE_CON_CNT; i++, j++)
 		clk_save[j] = mmio_read_32(CRU_BASE + CRU_CLKGATE_CON(i));
 
-	clk_save[j] = mmio_read_32(PHP_CRU_BASE + PHPCRU_CLKGATE_CON);
+	clk_save[j++] = mmio_read_32(PHP_CRU_BASE + PHPCRU_CLKGATE_CON);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < SECURECRU_CLKGATE_CON_CNT; i++, j++)
 		clk_save[j] = mmio_read_32(SCRU_BASE + SECURECRU_CLKGATE_CON(i));
@@ -235,7 +235,7 @@ void clk_gate_con_restore(void)
 			      WITH_16BITS_WMSK(clk_save[j]));
 
 	mmio_write_32(PHP_CRU_BASE + PHPCRU_CLKGATE_CON,
-		      WITH_16BITS_WMSK(clk_save[j]));
+		      WITH_16BITS_WMSK(clk_save[j++]));
 
 	for (i = 0; i < SECURECRU_CLKGATE_CON_CNT; i++, j++)
 		mmio_write_32(SCRU_BASE + SECURECRU_CLKGATE_CON(i),
-- 
